DATA & ARCHIVAL CREDITS:

1. Raw Airborne LiDAR Point Clouds & Canopy Height Models (CHM):
   Cook, B. D., Corp, L. A., Nelson, R. F., Middleton, E. M., Morton, D. C.,
   McCorkel, J. T., Masek, J. G., Ranson, K. J., Ly, V., & Montesano, P. M. (2013).
   NASA Goddard's LiDAR, Hyperspectral and Thermal (G-LiHT) Airborne Imager
   (AMIGA-Carb Mexico Campaign, April–May 2013). U.S. Government Public Domain
   (https://glihtdata.gsfc.nasa.gov/).

2. Reprocessed 0.33 m Bare-Earth DEMs, G1 Visualizations & Classified Ground (.laz):
   Britton, B. (2026). G-LiHT Yucatan East & West 2013: Reprocessed Ground Points,
   DEMs and Visualizations. Distributed by OpenTopography under Creative Commons
   Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0):
   - https://doi.org/10.5069/G9TH8JX9 (East)
   - https://doi.org/10.5069/G9Z899N1 (West)
   Methodology: Britton, B. et al. (2025), Journal of Archaeological Method and
   Theory (https://doi.org/10.1007/s10816-025-09741-5).

3. Primary Archaeological & Remote Sensing Literature (`papers/`):
   Included for scholarly verification and fair-use research reference; copyright
   remains with the respective authors, UNAM (Estudios de Cultura Maya), Centro
   INAH Chiapas / Bolom, Elsevier (JAS: Reports), and Taylor & Francis.
